Below is a summary of what’s happening and a targeted fix in lib/features/copy-paste/BpmnCopyPaste.js to preserve external‐label DI when you copy & paste (so that your event labels “A” and “B” will survive the pool→process extraction).

1) Bug analysis  
   - When you call `copyPaste.copy([ ... shapes ... ])`, Diagram-JS will also pick up the external label “shapes” behind the scenes.  
   - In our BPMN‐specific hook ( BpmnCopyPaste.js ) we bail out early when `isLabel(descriptor)` is true, but we never copy the label’s DI (its bounds x/y/width/height).  
   - As a result, on paste there is no label geometry and the labels simply don’t render.

2) Fix  
   - In the `copyPaste.copyElement` listener, right before we `return descriptor` for labels, grab the original `businessObject.di.label` bounds and stash them onto the descriptor (`descriptor.x/y/width/height`).  
   - Diagram-JS’ generic paste logic will pick up those numbers and lay the label out correctly.

